From 079bc588534b97466167704784253f112ab98107 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: khj1222 <39723594+khj1222@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 20:01:36 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] displacement_tta: transport Copy direction-prior components
 with the spatial transform

Mirror and rotate3 TTA transform every input channel spatially and, on the
way back, negate or reorder the *output* displacement components so the
variants agree in the original frame. The two ZYX direction priors in the
Copy model's 8-channel input (channels 2:5 and 5:8) are vectors too, but
their components were left alone: after a z flip the prior still pointed
+z in a volume that now runs the other way, so each variant answered a
different question and the merge averaged them.

run_model_tta gains `input_vector_channel_starts`, empty by default, and
predict_displacement passes (2, 5) only when the checkpoint config has
use_triplet_direction_priors and the input is the 8-channel layout. Every
other caller is byte-for-byte unchanged.

Tests: a model that returns its own input priors now comes back with
those priors after TTA in both modes (max error 2.4e-7 against 3.04 and
2.45 before); scalar channels, the input tensor, unconfigured callers and
other channel widths are untouched; out-of-range groups are rejected.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
